      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "There is a risk of bias, but for client-facing roles, the perception of professionalism is a critical tangible asset rather than just subjective flavor. Even with identical content, a polished tone signals to a company that the candidate can mirror corporate culture and maintain a trusted brand image reliably. While someone with less formal speaking habits *can* learn to adapt, assuming they lack the competence for high-level tasks simply because of their initial speech style often overlooks their actual ability to edit themselves when the stakes are higher.",
